|ID = 781
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Mamoluga
|name2 = Mamolan Pasalan
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mamolan Pasalan''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
This form is <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other cats from Tales of the Nekoluga, this cat is not meant to be used until it evolves.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Interestingly, this unit acts as a base defender. Mamolan Pasalan functions similarly to the likes of [[Meditation Cat (Special Cat)|Paragon Cat]], but with [[Weaken]] instead of [[Knockback]], better stats, and Area Attack. However, the necessity of such a role is questionable, as it lacks application everywhere outside of this intended niche. Mamolan Pasalan is primarily useful in luring strategies that revolve around isolating a specific enemy in order to quickly beat them to a bloody pulp. Its Weaken has around a 46% uptime at 6.67 seconds (55% uptime/8 seconds against [[Fruit Treasures|Fruited]] traits), which is more than good enough to let you burst down specific threats without retaliation, or potentially build up other attackers. Mamolan Pasalan's [[Conjure]] can also be used to cover for it when enemies start getting too close for comfort, acting as a sort of panic button with good burst damage and high pierce.

This manner of playstyle is very situational, however, and requires actively trying to maximize Mamolan Pasalan's value. Outside of these niche strategies, it can act as a source of general base-defense for when frontline maintenance fails; being practically immortal outside of high-piercing enemies, there's little chance of it dying under normal circumstances. It also sees usage in Zombie-centric stages, since many have a tendency to burrow past all of your frontline attackers directly onto your Cat Base, where Mamolan Pasalan is actively waiting to get the jump on them.

Even with all of this, the way Mamolan Pasalan is designed tends to fall flat a lot of the time, even in its intended spot of play. For one, despite being immortal against ordinary enemies, it is severely susceptible to pierce of any kind due to a lack of immunities. Second, the only thing this unit provides is the Weaken debuff, which is hardly a game-changer in 90% of circumstances. All in all, Mamolan Pasalan is situational at the best of times, requiring you to work around it, which usually isn't worth the hastle.

